From df54d0207705ffb9033efa35ad7a76a544ee1b88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:55:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(inventory): present authored native containers

Bind authored container geometry to authoritative Java menus, slots and cursor state without changing inventory request ownership.

CPU geometry, original-machine probes and meaningful widget interaction
tests establish these bounded behaviors; native GPU/font-family parity,
live container transfers and complete custom responses remain separate gates.

Share bounded native scene, layout, image and text primitives between modal
forms and real container presentation. Negotiate a separate container
program, bound to the current connection, actual ChestMenu object, menu ID
and increasing sequence. Retain vanilla stacks, carried items, state
revisions, click/release/quickcraft dispatch and same-menu close semantics.
Use the same clipped native slot rectangle for rendering and pointer hits.

Reproduce pinned native progress and transient slot-to-slot flight consumers
through authored flags and real menu state changes. Keep typed count labels
at their authored bounds with Java count formatting once; vanilla retains
carried decorations. Read exact retained native lock bytes and the owned
connection's showTags rule. Unknown required storage/filter presentation or
unsupported visible renderers keeps the complete stock container screen.
No cursor collection, item snapshot, native request address or false
inactive-item binding is manufactured for presentation.

Reject visible inventory buttons with unsupported action mappings before
enabling native presentation; retain the stock screen instead of inert
controls. Split tooltip components on actual newlines even without an
authored width. Normalize CRLF across styled runs and preserve empty lines,
colors, emphasis and bounded wrapping without rewriting literal escapes.

Original target index and fresh scheduler fixtures cover explicit, hidden
and percentage sizes. Java layout regressions cover positions, anchors,
offsets, constraints, malformed coordinates and unchanged template cells.
Visit only actual bounded children; retain strict container completeness
until intentional authored subsets receive a separate admission review.
Native pixels, actor delivery and live Social presentation remain open.

Original 1.26.51.1/build 51061372 vector updater execution establishes
coefficient interpolation, progress clamps, the duration floor and signed
offsets. All 1,536 mixed-unit native samples across 32 easing selectors
match the add-on within 1.5e-4 after layout resolution. Targeted tests cover
viewport changes, hit bounds, reset/play and dependent dimensions. Native
GPU comparison, container animation lifecycle and the other output types
remain open requirements; these CPU checks do not establish GUI parity.

Share the native animation manager with authored container scenes. Dispatch
entrance-push and scrollbar events, relayout animated size/offset controls,
and retain clocks across authoritative binding refreshes by hierarchical
control and inventory identity. Newly inserted controls start at the update
time; removed and destroyed controls retire without losing slot addresses.

Pinned Bedrock 1.26.51.1 ui_common.json defines the container entrance
offset and player-portrait size tracks. Zero-size entrance frames retain
their authoritative slot mapping while rejecting pointer input. Inventory
item and flight opacity is carried with each extracted GUI item and applied
at the final atlas or oversized texture blit with premultiplied tint, so
cached textures and ordinary Java item users remain independent.

Targeted lifecycle, container refresh, animated picking, scrolling, and
premultiplied vertex tests pass. Exit/pop transitions, carried-item opacity,
inactive filters, broader workstation coverage, and native/direct/proxy
visual parity remain required; this does not establish full GUI coverage.

Resolve color animation references and run four-channel image-component
tracks through the shared forms, HUD and container renderer. Keep easing
overshoot until final color submission, multiply image color alpha by
control opacity once, and retain color clocks across binding refreshes.

Accept version-3 storage scenes for hopper, dispenser, dropper, barrel,
ender chest and shulker box menus. Match the real Java menu family and
slot count before claiming ownership, then reuse the native scene and
actual-slot geometry with ordinary inventory packet authority. Retain
the original screen object only for failure recovery; never synthesize
a chest screen for another menu type. Preserve count-one activation,
contents ordering, replacement lifetime and stale-menu rejection.

Register the separate bidirectional native furnace preference channel and
retain tab, filter and layout choices per family across screen openings.
Discard queued updates and disconnect callbacks from an older connection,
and clear preferences when their owner disconnects. Keep unknown native
enum values intact, and send edits only when the server advertises the
channel. This prepares native furnace controllers; the cooking scenes and
their native/direct/ViaProxy comparisons remain incomplete.

Bind container payloads, pending contents, action acknowledgments and
click authority to the current ClientPacketListener. Java reconfiguration
can reuse a physical connection, menu number and sequence. Begin a new
play session explicitly and reject retired receivers and disconnects
before they consume its pending presentation or send inventory actions.
Tests cover reconfiguration on the same connected transport, reused menu
identity, delayed contents and acknowledgments, and session cleanup.

Present the bundled brewing-stand program over the actual five-slot menu.
Keep normal Java inventory operations and receive signed native progress
counters separately from Java short properties. Bind every update to the
play listener, menu object, kind and presentation sequence; retired updates
cannot change a newly opened workstation. Resolve singleton fuel and input
cells alongside the three bottle cells and all player inventory slots.

Receive authoritative cooking snapshots and raw progress in the production
client. Bind retained state to the exact play listener, menu object, family
and monotonic opening/update identities. Reject stale frames before item
conversion, retire old authority on a malformed newer frame, and retain
the sequence floor when a menu closes so reused IDs cannot revive it.

Share ordinary container and cooking presentation frames over the real
menu renderer. Copy translated recipe previews, keep their references
separate from inventory slots, and retain raw progress without changing
item authority. Tests resolve all 39 inventory slots through real layout
and cover menu reuse, reconnects, invalid conversion and progress updates.

Keep ordinary cooking controls for scenes with required input that is not
yet implemented. Complete cursor semantics, search/navigation and the
remaining authored handlers before replacing the default cooking screen.

Match authored close commands to their source input and pressed mapping.
Cooking slot buttons also map menu_cancel to try_menu_exit; that mapping
must not close a menu on an ordinary primary or secondary pointer click.
Use one clipped, front-to-back control order for close buttons and slots,
including equal-layer overlays, disabled controls and transparent frames.
A headless screen regression covers both pointer buttons on 63 real menu
slots with the cooking cancel mapping and fails with the original handler.
Native cooking activation and remaining controls are still incomplete.

Negotiate typed cooking action and result payloads in the Fabric play
session. Retain the original cell and snapshot through follow-up phases,
including synchronous bridge replies and newer predicted frames. Admit
initial input only after resolving its authored scope. Match replies to
the complete action, serialize independent gestures, and require a newer
frame after rejected or consumed authority. Retire pending input after
capability withdrawal, menu replacement, transport ambiguity or timeout.
Keep request floors across same-listener menu reuse.

Default cooking programs still use ordinary controls. This client transport
does not establish native device equivalence, cross-input prediction,
completed default controls or native visual parity. Regression tests exercise the
state transitions without a GPU or a live server.

Route admitted authored recipe cells through the production sender and
bind action authority to the installed native screen. Carry the resolved
recipe scope into clipped front-to-back geometry. Consume captured button
presses, drags, releases and duplicate releases independently of vanilla
inventory dispatch; retain the original cell when newer frames replace it.
Declare Java primary/secondary pointer presses as phase zero and releases
as phase two. Native physical device equivalence remains unverified.

Retain a one-shot terminal release after retirement or ambiguous transport
so a failed presentation cannot strand a primary gesture. Release only on
the same connected listener and actual menu, preserve increasing request
identity, and never retry an ambiguous terminal send. Restore the exact
original screen even after controller ownership retires, without replacing
another screen or a reused menu. Keep unsupported required controls and
nonempty-cursor branches on the ordinary menu rather than installing an
inert authored view. The default search/navigation/help controls, focus,
tertiary/controller bindings and complete native presentation stay open.

Headless integration tests execute resolved authored cells, the real sender,
frame replacement, same-menu restoration, capability withdrawal and
ambiguous-send cleanup. Disabling pointer routing fails the new interaction
regression. These controls do not prove live primary transfer acceptance,
GPU output or native physical input parity.

Reject unsupported recipe mapping attributes and require actual boolean
flags. The pointer adapter cannot honor select/deselect constraints and
must not turn those mappings into an unconditional recipe transfer. Both
the missing-attribute guard and string-boolean acceptance are covered by
the authored geometry regression.

Route supported navigation and filtering toggles through the existing
per-family preference transport. Resolve their real authored group/index
and checked state, keep clipped painter order with slots and recipes,
and wait for a newer matching cooking snapshot before accepting more
input. Do not interrupt pending recipe gestures. Capability loss, timeout
and ambiguous preference sends restore the exact original menu screen.

The unchanged target callbacks146c99520 and146c99b40 pass 74 controls
over supplied controller/model state, with downstream tab/filter setters,
collection rebuild and settings refresh observed at their call boundary.
Their event index and checked fields remain distinct. Pointer handlers
cover current selection, filtered state, pending snapshots and failure
recovery. Layout, focus, search and controller mappings remain unfinished;
unsupported required controls continue to use ordinary screens.
